# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CWICK .gitignore
#
# Rule of thumb: source, docs, and the small generated asset that lets a plain
# checkout build (`src/webui_embed.c`) are tracked; everything a build, a
# benchmark or a run produces stays out. The model weights alone are 300+ GiB,
# so those heavy paths are excluded explicitly. tools/ is the exception: it
# mixes sources and binaries sharing a base name, so it uses a whitelist.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- tools/ ----------------------------------------------------------------
# tools/ holds portable harness sources (.c/.m/.sh/.py) next to the Mach-O
# executables built from them, often with the same base name. Ignore the whole
# subtree and whitelist anything with a suffix: an extension-less binary has
# nothing to whitelist, so it stays out automatically, including tools added
# in a later session. Listing one name per binary here proved unreliable.
/tools/**
!/tools/
!/tools/**/
!/tools/*.*
!/tools/**/*.*

# Scratch output from the harnesses: measured dumps and kept backups are local
# artefacts, not shipped sources. These follow the whitelist so they win over
# the "anything with a suffix" negation above.
/tools/**/*.csv
/tools/**/*.dat
/tools/**/*.tmp
/tools/**/*.bak
/tools/**/*.orig

# Verify with
#   git status --short --untracked-files=all -- tools/
# which should only ever list new source and script files.

# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------------
# Kept after the tools/ whitelist on purpose: a negation above would otherwise
# pull a compiled artifact that has a suffix (tools/*.o, a .dSYM bundle) back
# into git status. The last matching rule wins.
/cwick
/tests/test_cwick
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
*.dSYM/
*.metallib
*.exe
*.out
a.out
*.gcno
*.gcda
core
core.*

# src/webui_embed.c is generated by tools/embed_web but stays tracked on
# purpose, so `make` works from a fresh clone without running the generator.

# --- model weights and checkpoint material ---------------------------------
# Full GLM-5.3-Flash (~306 GiB) and any checkpoint fetched with
# download_model.sh. Never in git history: a clone must not try to fetch them.
/zai-org/
/deepseek-ai/
/MiniMaxAI/
/models/
*.safetensors
*.safetensors.index.json
*.gguf
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.incomplete

# --- runtime state ---------------------------------------------------------
# Prefix-cache KV snapshots (~217 MiB per 1000 prompt tokens).
/pfxcache/
*.pfx

# Per-app SQLite databases plus the auth store: they hold password and API-key
# hashes, and each app writes its own file next to its code.
/dbs/
apps/**/*.db
apps/**/*.db-wal
apps/**/*.db-shm
apps/**/*.db-journal
apps/**/*.sqlite
apps/**/*.sqlite3

# --- benchmarks and logs ---------------------------------------------------
# .bench/ holds local profiling runs: multi-hundred-megabyte logs, KV caches
# and one-off harnesses with machine-specific paths. The portable harnesses
# live in tools/ instead.
/.bench/
*.log
*.trace
# Kept backups of a run log do not end in .log, so the rule above misses them
# (`cwick-serve.log.orig-<date>`, `...log.pre-<change>`). They hold whole
# prompts and are the single largest thing in the tree after the weights.
/logs/

# --- local notes -----------------------------------------------------------
# The working spec: requirements and target numbers that change from session to
# session. Kept beside the code on purpose, but untracked.
/goal.md

# Methodology notes for building this kind of runtime, kept locally: the
# markdown is long-lived reference material for whoever works on the engine,
# not part of what the repository ships.
/skills/
/expert/

# The same notes are copied into the expert package under expert/skills/, and
# the pattern above is anchored to the repository root, so it does not reach
# them. Same reasoning: reference material, not shipped source. The rest of
# expert/ (agent definitions, avatars, plugin.json) stays visible on purpose --
# that is the part worth diffing when the methodology changes.
/expert/skills/


# --- editor / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# --- local secrets ---------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
